==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etym|gml|de}} {{term|helfte|lang=gml}}, which pertains to Middle Low German {{term|half||half|lang=gml}}. The form entered early modern German via [[Central German]]. The alternation ''-b-'' ↔ ''-ft-'' between {{term|halb|lang=de}} and ''Hälfte'' has not been levelled, probably because the same alternation occurs also—for different reasons—in native [[High German]] words (compare {{term|schreiben|lang=de}} ↔ {{term|Schrift|lang=de}}). Cognate with {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|helft|lang=nl}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈhɛlftə/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-Hälfte.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f||Hälften}}

# [[half]]; fifty [[percent]] of something
# [[half]], [[share]]; any of two [[correlate|correlating]] [[piece]]s, whatever the size
#: {{usex|Ich will die größere '''Hälfte'''!|I want the bigger '''half'''!|lang=de}}

